.TH AUDIT-PUBLIC-SURFACE 1 2026-09-01 "just3ws" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audit-public-surface \- review public content and built output for privacy and topology risks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-report-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb
\fB\-\-decide\fR \fIID=DECISION\fR
.br
.B ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb
\fB\-\-completion\fR \fIzsh|bash\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The auditor reviews documented public-content roots and the built \fI_site/\fR boundary. It detects credential-shaped values, direct personal data, health and family context, private workplace details, uncertain recollections, local paths, internal project files, backlog routes, and quarantined AI pages missing noindex metadata.
.PP
Normal mode creates a redacted local review queue. Strict mode fails on critical findings and unresolved high-risk or quarantined findings. A finding is a review prompt, not a verdict. Human judgment remains the publication gate.
.SH WORKFLOW
.nf
source -> sanitize -> build -> audit -> human decision -> publish
                                      |                 |
                                      +-> hold ----------+
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I tmp/public-surface-audit/report.json
Local redacted report. This path is ignored and must not be published.
.TP
.I tmp/public-surface-audit/decisions.json
Local decisions keyed by finding identifier.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb
ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb --strict --json
ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb --decide ID=generalize
ruby bin/audit_public_surface.rb --completion zsh > /tmp/_audit_public_surface
.fi
